WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:03.230
"Fast X" made off with millions in its opening
weekend.

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:07.982
Here's how the film maintained the franchise's
box office muscle, ten movies deep.

00:00:08.505 --> 00:00:12.500
Longtime fans of "The Fast and the Furious"
franchise tend to make an event out of the

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.103
debut of each new chapter.

00:00:14.103 --> 00:00:19.111
"Fast X" is the 10th film in the main series
and 11th overall, putting "Fast" movies in

00:00:19.111 --> 00:00:23.800
a rare class with long-running franchises
like "Star Wars," "Star Trek," the Marvel

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.449
Cinematic Universe, and James Bond.

00:00:26.449 --> 00:00:31.720
Though there might not be "Fast" TV tie-ins
on the scale of "Star Wars" or the MCU, the

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.897
series nevertheless has a loyal and active
fandom that has historically shown up on opening weekend.

00:00:36.897 --> 00:00:42.200
From 2009's "Fast and Furious" onward, the
"Fast" movies have all raked in at least $60

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.546
million domestically in the first weekend
of their theatrical run.

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:47.366
"Liquid gold!"

00:00:48.761 --> 00:00:54.559
2015's "Furious 7" was the biggest of the
bunch, banking nearly $150 million in its

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:55.840
first three days.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.230
Every other installment has come in respectably
but still under $100 million.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:04.110
Six of the "Fast" films with big opening weekends
went on to gross more than half a billion

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:08.000
dollars worldwide, so things look good for
"Fast X" on the whole.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.340
That said, two factors throw a wrench into
what would otherwise be unqualified success.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:18.720
The $67.5 million domestic take for "Fast
X" is the second lowest since "Fast and Furious,"

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.630
beating only the side project, "Fast and Furious
Presents: Hobbs and Shaw," which debuted with

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:25.460
about $60 million.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:31.310
The latest film's $340 million production
budget also far exceeds the rest of the franchise,

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:36.590
which means "Fast X" will have to do much
better by the end of its run just to break even.

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:41.200
"Fast X" might not have lit the domestic box
office on fire, but its international receipts

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.560
are smoking hot.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:48.280
The film's $318.9 million global total is
the second best of the year so far behind

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:49.980
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie."

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:55.775
When taking the U.S. figure out of the equation,
it's the single best international debut of 2023.

00:01:55.775 --> 00:01:59.969
Worldwide ticket sales are where the "Fast"
films have managed to hold steady and even

00:01:59.969 --> 00:02:03.700
make gains, while sci-fi and superhero franchises
have struggled lately.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:08.140
To paint a better picture, let's compare "Fast
X" and "Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania."

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:14.590
"Fast X" grossed more than $250 million internationally
in its first weekend, while the third "Ant-Man"

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.480
film barely crossed $100 million.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:22.360
"Fast X" did particularly well in China, but
it also performed admirably in Italy and Brazil,

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:26.044
two countries that serve as locations in the
globetrotting action film.

00:02:26.044 --> 00:02:27.590
"All right, dorks, what are we blowing up?

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:28.090
What?

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:29.392
The Vatican?"

00:02:29.508 --> 00:02:35.180
More proof that spectacle — in this case,
spectacular car chases, physics-defying stunts,

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:37.650
and epic explosions — is a universal language?

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.099
"Fast X" had a strong opening on IMAX screens.

00:02:41.099 --> 00:02:45.879
The film made about $22 million from the more
expensive tickets sold for that format, and

00:02:45.879 --> 00:02:51.004
the majority of IMAX ticket sales, $16.2 million,
came from overseas.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.000
"Fast X" benefitted from the fact that it
hit theaters at the very beginning of the

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:00.230
summer movie season, before the marquees got
too crowded with big-name blockbusters.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:05.849
One reason for its $318.9 million worldwide
opening is simply a lack of competition.

00:03:05.849 --> 00:03:10.379
It's been seven weeks since "The Super Mario
Bros. Movie" hit screens, so the majority

00:03:10.379 --> 00:03:13.879
of viewers who wanted to see the video game
adaptation have already seen it.

00:03:13.879 --> 00:03:19.080
"Mario" is also available to rent or purchase
via video-on-demand by now, which likely steered

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.459
even more moviegoers to "Fast X."

00:03:21.459 --> 00:03:25.560
"Guardians of the Galaxy: Vol. 3" has been
holding its own at the box office, nearing

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.939
the $700 million mark in worldwide ticket
sales.

00:03:28.939 --> 00:03:32.710
But its two-week head start made some room
for whatever audience overlap there is between

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:35.099
"Guardians 3" and "Fast X."

00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:40.170
Elsewhere down the list is R-rated fare such
as "Evil Dead Rise," which was in its fifth

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.799
week, and "John Wick: Chapter 4," in its ninth.

00:03:42.799 --> 00:03:47.200
There was also the warmer, fluffier "Book
Club: The Next Chapter" and "Are You There

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.492
God? It's Me, Margaret."

00:03:48.492 --> 00:03:53.459
Had "Fast X" contended with "The Flash," "Indiana
Jones and the Dial of Destiny," or "Mission:

00:03:53.459 --> 00:03:57.489
Impossible — Dead Reckoning Part One," it
may not have conquered the box office quite

00:03:57.489 --> 00:03:58.489
so handily.

00:03:59.226 --> 00:04:01.655
"Fast" movies have never been prestige cinema.

00:04:01.655 --> 00:04:06.489
Even so, about half of the entries in the
franchise have scored decently well with critics,

00:04:06.489 --> 00:04:09.370
with "Furious 7" and "Fast Five" coming in
at the top.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:13.209
It took a while for critics to catch on to
what audiences already knew.

00:04:13.209 --> 00:04:17.630
The early "Fast" films linger at the bottom
of Rotten Tomatoes' ranking, probably in part

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:21.990
because reviewers didn't have a sense of what
the over-the-top franchise was trying to do.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:25.910
Many of the positive comments pertaining to
the later films praise them for self-awareness

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:27.290
and sheer fun.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:31.370
Unfortunately for "Fast X," though, the critical
community is divided.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:35.060
Even those who had good things to say about
the film are mostly muted in their praise,

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:38.229
while those who disliked it haven't held back
with their complaints.

00:04:38.229 --> 00:04:42.370
Critics have compared it to sustaining a head
injury, referring to the script as something

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:44.240
that an eight-year-old could have written.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.460
Others simply call it loud and dumb.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:50.370
But that hasn't deterred fans who took to
Rotten Tomatoes and social media sites, where

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:51.710
they have the film's back.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:56.460
"Fast X" currently has an 86 percent audience
score compared to its 54 percent critical

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.190
Tomatometer rating.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:01.370
Viewers seem to appreciate the plot twists
as well as the non-stop action.

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:05.880
And since the general public is who's buying
the tickets and the popcorn, especially for

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:10.230
a deep-into-the-franchise movie like "Fast
X," they're a better predictor of a movie's

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:11.230
bottom line.

00:05:12.047 --> 00:05:16.420
One thing that most critics and fans agree
on is that Jason Momoa is a worthwhile addition

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.177
to "The Fast and the Furious" family.

00:05:18.177 --> 00:05:22.830
From Vin Diesel and Jason Statham to John
Cena and Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson, the sprawling

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:26.110
cast was already pretty full up on middle-aged
muscly men.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:31.130
The 43-year-old Momoa, who also plays Aquaman,
is arguably a similar type of actor.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:35.189
They don't always get credit for their craft,
and if we're being honest, fans don't really

00:05:35.189 --> 00:05:38.240
come to see their movies for humanistic performances
in the first place.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:42.110
And like with the DCEU, the franchise itself
is the brand name.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:47.300
Like many of his cohorts, Momoa is a well-liked
celebrity who audiences are happy to see in

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:51.340
movies, but whether he was a reliable box
office draw was still an open question.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:55.440
It's not necessarily Momoa's star power that
convinced viewers to come out for "Fast X";

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:59.150
more likely it was the strong buzz he earned
for his performance as the series' newest

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:00.860
villain, Dante Reyes.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:05.930
The actor told Variety that he conceived of
Reyes as an androgynous, vengeful peacock.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:06.983
"I'm Dante.

00:06:06.983 --> 00:06:07.983
Enchante."

00:06:08.347 --> 00:06:13.110
The son of the drug lord slain in "Fast Five,"
Reyes has a predilection for nail polish and

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:14.110
colorful cars.

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:18.729
While critics, fans, and Momoa himself acknowledge
that the performance is over-the-top, the

00:06:18.729 --> 00:06:20.550
consensus is that's a good thing.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:24.220
Dante Reyes is an entertaining presence who
steals the movie.

00:06:24.341 --> 00:06:26.531
Also, the rest of the cast is stacked.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:31.530
While "The Fast and the Furious" films feature
more than their fair share of standout action

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:36.720
set pieces, arguably only a few of the 11
installments have risen to the level of legitimately

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:43.430
good filmmaking. 2011's "Fast Five" and 2015's
"Furious 7" are frequently cited as the franchise's

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:44.430
high points.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:49.650
"Fast X" director Louis Leterrier told Entertainment
Weekly that the fifth film is "easily the

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:53.650
best," and his 10th film is essentially a
direct "Fast Five" sequel.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:57.830
Leterrier reframes the infamous safe chase
by adding in the perspective of Dante Reyes,

00:06:57.830 --> 00:07:01.639
who is knocked off a bridge in Rio while his
father, Hernan, is killed.

00:07:01.639 --> 00:07:06.110
This becomes the motivation for Momoa's character,
who wants justice for his father's death and

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:08.050
the loss of his family's fortune.

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:11.940
Dipping back into past narratives and even
changing what the audience has seen before

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:16.320
is a tactic that "The Fast and the Furious"
series has employed again and again, often

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:17.500
with crowd-pleasing results.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:22.210
Since the word was out that "Fast X" had strong
connections to "Fast Five," it's reasonable

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:26.449
to think some fans, perhaps even some who
haven't kept up with the entire series, showed

00:07:26.449 --> 00:07:28.750
up to see how the former would tie into the
latter.

00:07:29.496 --> 00:07:33.440
Even some of the "Fast" franchise's most ardent
supporters thought that the film series may

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.670
have finally jumped the shark with "F9," a
movie in which, among other physics and logic-defying

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:42.262
feats, Tej and Roman enter actual space in
a rocket car.

00:07:42.424 --> 00:07:44.458
"Man, this is insane.

00:07:44.458 --> 00:07:45.791
We are headed to outer space.

00:07:45.791 --> 00:07:49.428
You acting like we on the way to Home Depot."

00:07:49.428 --> 00:07:53.849
What started as a standalone film about street
racing based on a real piece of investigative

00:07:53.849 --> 00:07:58.690
journalism has become an ever more purposefully
unbelievable collage of cinematic stunts,

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:01.930
with each subsequent sequel feeling the pressure
to up the ante.

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:06.830
"Fast X" tones things down ever so slightly,
but we're still a long way from good old-fashioned

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:08.860
drag racing in downtown Los Angeles.

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:14.240
And that's more than okay with fans: They've
come to expect ridiculous, death-defying hijinks

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:18.009
that either wouldn't work in the first place
or would absolutely kill a human being who

00:08:18.009 --> 00:08:19.940
wasn't wearing franchise plot armor.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:23.160
"If it could be done in a car, they did it.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:28.720
If it violates the laws of god and gravity,
they did it twice."

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:33.580
Yes, "Fast X" is more kinetic energy than
comprehensible plot, and yes, there's some

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:37.909
egregious superheroification of the characters
as well as obvious fan service.

00:08:37.909 --> 00:08:42.339
But is anyone going to a "Fast and the Furious"
sequel this deep into the franchise hoping

00:08:42.339 --> 00:08:43.507
for subtlety?

00:08:43.507 --> 00:08:44.507
We think not.

00:08:44.507 --> 00:08:49.050
Even those who can't help but point out how
nonsensical the movie is also can't stop themselves

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:50.050
from enjoying it.

00:08:50.706 --> 00:08:54.040
If there's one thing people know about "The
Fast and the Furious" — including people

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:57.720
who've never seen a single film in the series
— it's that, even more than they are about

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.080
cars, these movies are about family.

00:09:00.323 --> 00:09:01.703
"I don't have friends.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:03.910
I got family."

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:08.070
For an in-joke to work itself into the culture
so thoroughly that practically everyone gets

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:10.410
it, the "Fast" franchise must be doing something
right.

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:14.690
"Fast X" not only utters the word more times
than viewers can count, but it also makes

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:19.480
good on its central theme, exploring the bonds
between fathers and sons especially.

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:24.410
The Toretto family tree is pretty twisty and
branchy, and allegiances turn on a dime whenever

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.769
the plot requires it.

00:09:25.769 --> 00:09:29.720
For a franchise that’s been going strong
for over two decades, it’s become a necessary

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:31.230
part of the design.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:35.350
One way to think of the "Fast" movies is as
a gritty, testosterone-fueled, big-budget

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:36.350
soap opera.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:39.730
Fans that have stuck with the series follow
their favorite characters and try to guess

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:41.940
who will backstab or make amends with who.

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:46.850
For all the slingshotted cars and races against
trains, these movies do have a human element

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:51.880
to them, and one that's surprisingly earnest,
particularly when compared to other hyper-masculine,

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:53.570
high-octane action movies.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:57.589
Maybe all that fire and metal gives audiences
the cover they need to enjoy what's really

00:09:57.589 --> 00:09:59.603
just a sappy story at heart.

00:10:00.098 --> 00:10:04.110
The biggest box office successes of all time
— the "Fast" films among them — almost

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:08.030
all have something in common: They're rated
PG-13.

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:12.470
The PG-13 rating stretches from the later
installments in the "Harry Potter" franchise

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:18.017
to the most recent "Guardians of the Galaxy"
movie, which features the MCU's first-ever F-bomb.

00:10:18.017 --> 00:10:21.557
It's not exactly an informative measure of
a film's family friendliness.

00:10:21.557 --> 00:10:25.910
But generally speaking, it affords families
(at least those with slightly older children)

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:29.540
the ability to take everyone to the movie
theater for the night.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:32.910
That typically gives an automatic boost to
PG-13 titles.

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:37.279
Teens and adults won't always seek out G or
PG films on their own, while younger audiences

00:10:37.279 --> 00:10:39.320
are prohibited from movies that receive an
R-rating.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:44.840
"Fast X" and its PG-13 rating falls squarely
in line with other broadly appealing box office

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:50.730
behemoths like "Avatar," "Titanic," "Star
Wars," "Jurassic Park," and last year's big

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:52.440
hit, "Top Gun: Maverick."

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:57.410
In a cultural atmosphere where identity politics
can quickly derail a film's mass appeal, "Fast

00:10:57.410 --> 00:10:59.649
X" manages to remain uncontroversial.

00:10:59.649 --> 00:11:03.440
That helped its performance at home, where,
admittedly, the franchise has been stalling

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:07.779
out a bit, and it certainly helped abroad,
where big-budget films have to play ball with

00:11:07.779 --> 00:11:10.000
some countries' conservative censors.

